    "body": "## Problem\n\nWith speculative decoding, SGLang annotates each decode round as two iteration spans: the draft-model step and the target verify step.\n\n```\nstep[DRAFT bs=2 g_sq=16 g_sqsq=128 g_sqsk=22944 g_sk=2868 forward_id=14960]\nstep[VERIFY bs=2 g_sq=16 g_sqsq=128 g_sqsk=670032 g_sk=83754 forward_id=15173]\n```\n\nThese labels come from builds whose `build_step_span_name` names the target-verify step `VERIFY` and every draft-model step `DRAFT`. Both steps carry `g_` aggregates.\n\n`SGLANG_DETAILED_PATTERN` only matches `EXTEND`, `DECODE` and `MIXED`, so on these traces only the prefill steps become iteration roots. I tested on a real draft-model benchmark trace (TP rank 0, 9.2M events, concurrency 8). The splitter found 11 `EXTEND` roots, and only 36% of the GPU work fell inside their spans. Root detection graded the split `DEGRADED`, and `split_trace` printed *Refusing to split*. As a result, the trace yields no steady-state window.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Match `DRAFT` and `VERIFY` in `SGLANG_DETAILED_PATTERN`. They are listed in a new `SGLANG_SPECULATIVE_MODES` constant.\n- Parse both as generation steps, the same way as `DECODE`. Each one serves requests that are already past their prompt.\n\nOn the same trace, `split_trace --find-steady-state --llm-inference --CONC 8` now finds 501 roots and grades the split `SPLITTABLE`. The roots cover 97.4% of the GPU work, and 95.1% of that falls inside their spans. It writes a 32-step `decode_only` steady-state window at concurrency 8, plus the `mixed` and `prefilldecode` windows.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `TARGET_VERIFY` is deliberately not matched. The older roofline patches emit `step[TARGET_VERIFY ... c_...]`, and those traces already split today through the unknown-family path: `scheduler.run_batch` roots, 99.5% of the work inside spans, decode-only. `test_trace_split[sglang_mtp_speculative]` pins that path. I first tried matching `TARGET_VERIFY` as a known root, and that test caught a regression: it switched to roots